parts+=['## 2. General mathematical pattern','Temperature T(t) decreases toward fixed surrounding temperature S. The rate is proportional to the **difference** T-S, with the stated proportionality constant k>0, so dT/dt=-k(T-S). At T=S the derivative vanishes; above S it is negative. Intermediate or initial readings do not replace S or multiply k. Answer eligibility preserves the given named k; it is equality for arbitrary fixed k>0, not free reparameterization of a family. Otherwise replacing k by a positive numerical coefficient can be interpreted as a special model. Normal output adds “Write the equation in terms of the given constant k.” Raw source wording remains unchanged.','## 3. Complete component and bank map','Every source choice is mapped below, in captured field order. These are observed structural parameterizations, not a claim to recover author intent. All values are symbolic whole equations, so no arbitrary fitted scalar recipes are necessary. S=ambient; I=initial; SUM=I+S. k is the given fixed constant. The complete bank is always selected together.']
